<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico has assigned all three direct Cetes sales and one repurchase agreement whereby it sought to drain 730 million pesos from the secondary market on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    339 days   24.48 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    178 days   23.41 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     87 days   23.33 pct</p>
<p>The term and maturity of the repurchase agreement were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    280 million	1 day    22.33 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>((-- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
